Implement user story SKY-004-a: Express server routes, middleware, and module export

## Story Description
Implement src/server.ts with all route handlers (/health, /, /search, /cheapest), RAPIDAPI_KEY gating middleware, error handling, and proper module export separation so the app can be imported by tests without binding a port. FlightResult must be imported from SKY-002.

## Acceptance Criteria
- src/server.ts exports a named `app` (Express instance) separately from the `listen()` call so supertest can import it without binding a port
- The `listen()` call in src/server.ts is conditionally executed only when the file is run directly as the main entry point, not when imported as a module — `vitest run` must never bind a port
- GET /health returns HTTP 200 with Content-Type application/json and body matching { status: 'ok', uptime: <positive number> }; this endpoint is never gated by RAPIDAPI_KEY presence
- GET / returns HTTP 200 with Content-Type text/html and response body equal to the current contents of src/public/index.html as read from the file at request time — a hardcoded or inline HTML string in server.ts is not acceptable; modifying the file and restarting the server must cause GET / to return the updated content; this route is never gated by RAPIDAPI_KEY
- GET /search with valid query params returns HTTP 200 with body { flights: FlightResult[], count: number, searchedAt: ISO-8601 string } where count === flights.length and searchedAt reflects request time; missing required param (from, to, or date) → 400 { error }; non-numeric adults → 400 { error }; adults absent defaults to 1
- GET /cheapest with valid required params (from, to, date) returns HTTP 200 with the single cheapest FlightResult (price ≤ all others); empty results → 404 { error }; missing required param → 400 { error }; adults defaults to 1 if absent
- When RAPIDAPI_KEY env var is absent at server initialisation, GET /search and GET /cheapest return HTTP 503 { error: 'RAPIDAPI_KEY not configured' }; GET /health and GET / are unaffected
- When SkyscannerClient throws an error during /search or /cheapest, the server returns HTTP 500 { error: string } without crashing or emitting an unhandled promise rejection; FlightResult type is imported from SKY-002, not redeclared inline





